// The STM32H747's register map — ST's dual-core Cortex-M7/M4, as sysl constants.
//
// **Every line of sysl in this package but `tests.sysl` is generated.** It comes from ST's own
// `STM32H747_CM7.svd`, the CMSIS description shipped in Keil's STM32H7xx device family pack, by way of
// [sysl-lang/svd](https://github.com/sysl-lang/svd). Nothing generated should be hand-edited: a
// correction belongs in the generator or in a newer SVD, and anything typed in by hand is lost the next
// time the chip is regenerated. `README.md` records the exact command, the pack and the SVD's SHA-256.
//
// There is no `dependencies` block because this depends on nothing. It is constants.
//
// This is the block a *consumer* writes to reach this package:
//
//     dependencies {
//       stm32h747 { git = "github.com/sysl-lang/stm32h747", version = "0.1.0" }
//     }

package {
  name    = "stm32h747"
  version = "0.1.0"
  sysl    = "0.7.8"
}

// **There is no `requires` block and no `@link` directive.** It declares constants: base addresses,
// register offsets, field masks and shifts, and the names ST gives a field's values. No function, no
// storage, no C, so it is usable from a freestanding target with no heap — the only kind that wants it.
